>> title: Crisped Marinated Tofu
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: tofu, vegan, skillet, soy, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: crispy tofu, marinated tofu, baked tofu, pan-fried tofu, sesame tofu, tofu for bowls
>> pairs-with: coconut-rice, miso-ginger-dressing
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: press 30 min under a weight
>> step.2: marinate the cubes 20 min
>> step.3: toss in cornstarch
>> step.4: crisp 10 min, face by face, undisturbed
>> step.5: finish off the heat

Wrap @extra-firm tofu{14%oz}(400 g) in a folded towel, set a heavy pan on top and ~press{30%min}. What comes out is a quarter-cup of water and the room it leaves is what the marinade goes into. Skip this and the marinade sits on the outside, then boils off in the pan.

Cut @&(~1)pressed tofu{} into 1-in cubes and turn them through @soy sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @maple syrup{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @rice vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @garlic{2%cloves}(grated) and @ginger{1%tsp}(grated), then ~marinate{20%min}, turning once. Twenty minutes is the useful end of it — tofu is not meat and the marinade only ever reaches a few millimetres in, so an overnight soak buys nothing but a wetter cube to dry out again.

Lift @&(~1)marinated tofu{} out of the liquid, let it drip, and toss it in @cornstarch{2%Tbs} until each cube is dusty rather than pasty. The cornstarch takes up the marinade clinging to the surface and turns it into a shell; without it that same liquid just steams.

Crisp @&(~1)cornstarched tofu{} in @neutral oil{3%Tbs}(45 mL) in a wide #skillet{} over medium-high, ~fry{10%min} total, in one layer, **one face at a time and not stirred**. Give each face two and a half minutes and turn the cubes with tongs rather than shaking the pan. Stirring knocks the shell off before it sets, which is the single way this goes wrong.

Take the pan off the heat and toss @&(~1)crisped tofu{} with @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}(5 mL), @toasted sesame seeds{1%Tbs} and @scallions{2}(thin-sliced). Sesame oil on a hot burner goes flat and slightly rancid in under a minute; off the heat it stays nutty.
